# Document toolbar actions (Print / Download)

Print and Download PDF actions are **icon-only at all breakpoints**. Use `aria-label` and `title` for accessibility and tooltips.

## Markup

Wrap the action group in `doc-actions` (add page-specific class only if needed). Mark Print/Download with `icon-only-action`:

```tsx
<div className="button-row no-print doc-actions">
  <button
    type="button"
    className="button secondary icon-only-action"
    aria-label="Print"
    title="Print"
  >
    <Printer size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
    <span className="button-label">Print</span>
  </button>
  <button
    type="button"
    className="button icon-only-action"
    aria-label="Download PDF"
    title="Download PDF"
  >
    <Download size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
    <span className="button-label">PDF</span>
  </button>
</div>
```

## Required

- Add `icon-only-action` on Print/Download controls (buttons or links).
- Keep label text in `<span className="button-label">…</span>` (hidden by CSS; useful for screen readers that ignore aria inconsistently, and for future toggles).
- Always set `aria-label` and `title`.
- Mark decorative icons `aria-hidden="true"`.

## Do not

- Put Print/Download label text as a bare text node next to the icon.
- Apply `icon-only-action` to non-doc actions (Options, Start trip, Plan pickups, Scan, Crew).

## CSS

Shared rules live in `apps/web/app/globals.css` under `.doc-actions .button.icon-only-action`. Reuse those; do not invent per-page hide hacks.
